  "name": "Question 4",
  "problem": "Consider the following sets:\n\n$$\nA={n\\in N\u22232n+1<9},\\,B={n\\in N\u2223n\\ge 4}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- $A={1,2,3}$\n- $A\\cap B=\u2205$\n- $A$ and $B$ are disjoint",
  "worked_solution": "Two sets $A$ and $B$ are *disjoint* if they have no element in common, i.e., their intersection is empty:\n\n$$\nA\\cap B=\u2205\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that the elements of $A$ are positive integers that satisfy the inequality \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2n+1 & <9 \\\\ 2n & <8 \\\\ n & <4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our sets.\n\n- Statement I is true.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={n\\in N\u22232n+1<9} \\\\  & ={n\\in N\u2223n<4} \\\\  & ={1,2,3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B & ={n\\in N\u2223n\\ge 4} \\\\  & ={4,5,6,\u2026}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, the intersection is \n\n$$\nA\\cap B={1,2,3}\\cap {4,5,6,\u2026}=\u2205.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since the intersection is empty, the two sets are disjoint.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II and III.\"",
